{"text": "motherhood", "etymologies": [{"etymologyHTML": "<p>From Middle English <i class=\"Latn mention\" lang=\"enm\">moderhode</i>, <i class=\"Latn mention\" lang=\"enm\">moderhede</i>, equivalent to <i class=\"Latn mention\" lang=\"en\">mother</i> +\u200e <i class=\"Latn mention\" lang=\"en\">-hood</i>.\n</p>", "pos": [{"pos": "Noun", "definitions": [{"definition": "The state of being a mother.", "quote": [], "relative": {}}, {"definition": "Mothers, considered as a group.\n", "quote": [], "relative": {}}]}]}], "pronunciation": [["Received Pronunciation", "/\u02c8m\u028c\u00f0\u0259h\u028ad/"], ["General American", "/\u02c8m\u028c\u00f0\u025a\u02cch\u028ad/"]]}